@startuml

title Retrieval of a published market data set: four reads, one record

actor "Reader" as reader
participant "Screen" as screen
participant "Market data" as md
database "Publish record\nand its subject part" as publish
database "The candidate's points\nand their lineage" as points

== The list ==
reader -> screen : open the party's sets
screen -> md : list(subject, state, party, search)
md -> publish : the sets of the party,\nnewest first
md -> md : state from the columns;\nstaleness from the threshold
md --> screen : one row per set
screen --> reader : which set is in use, and what ended\nthe set before it

== The record ==
reader -> screen : open one set
screen -> md : record(subject, as-of)
md -> publish : the set the read rule selects
alt a set is published
  md -> points : the values of the set
  md --> screen : the header facts, the approval,\nthe state and the values
  screen --> reader : what the set says, and who put it there
else nothing is published
  md --> screen : a refusal naming the subject and the as-of
  screen --> reader : nothing was ever published
end

== The comparison ==
reader -> screen : compare two instants
screen -> md : record(the same subject, each as-of)
md --> screen : two sets, each with its own as-of
screen -> screen : the difference per node,\nand the nodes that appeared or dropped
screen --> reader : what changed, with the age of each side

== The values ==
note over screen, points
  A curve answers with its pillars, a forward set
  with its ladder, and a surface with a grid whose
  rows are expiries and whose columns are strikes.
  One smile is one row of the grid, not a second read.
end note
md -> points : read at the instant the record names
md --> screen : the points, the grid or one row of it

@enduml
